# XBD <dlfcn.h>
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The mode constants of <dlfcn.h>. dlopen() builds its mode from one
# relocation value and one visibility value, which needs the two pairs to
# be told apart and combinable. Each says why it has no mutant yet.

assertion  XBD.dlfcn.h.001
anchor     basedefs/dlfcn.h.html#DESCRIPTION/RTLD_LAZY
anchor     functions/dlopen.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       RTLD_LAZY differs from RTLD_NOW, RTLD_GLOBAL differs from RTLD_LOCAL,
           and neither RTLD_LAZY nor RTLD_NOW shares a bit with RTLD_GLOBAL or
           RTLD_LOCAL, so that one of each pair can be combined with | in the
           mode argument of dlopen().
note       dlopen() describes mode as a relocation value OR-ed with a visibility
           value. RTLD_LOCAL may be 0, so no value is required to be non-zero. That the pairs differ is
           inferred, not stated (Q-169).
test       t/001-rtld-modes.c
nomutant   compile-time check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants
